# Editor config. Untracked deliberately: without this, anything VS Code writes
# into .vscode/ — settings.json carrying local absolute paths, per-machine tasks —
# gets committed by the next `git add -A`, which is the actual risk here.
#
# The two files this dropped, extensions.json and launch.json, were Astro's own
# scaffolding: a recommendation to install the Astro extension, and a generic
# `astro dev` launch config. Neither held anything machine-specific, so if you
# want the extension hint back for contributors, keep the directory ignored and
# re-admit just that file:
#     !.vscode/extensions.json
.vscode/

# Scratch output from scripts/refresh-news.ts; uploaded to KV by CI, never committed.
.news-mirror/

# Scratch from scripts/set-tile-cache-headers.ts; removed on exit, never committed.
.tile-cache-headers/
